.SS "Execution Paths"
.TP
.B In-memory
(default when RAM is sufficient, or
.BR \-\-inmemory ).
All data structures live in RAM.  Realisations run in parallel via Rayon
with an auto-selected concurrency limit (4 threads, or 2 for N\~>\~10M;
overridable via
.BR \-\-threads ).
.TP
.B Streaming
(auto-selected when RAM is insufficient, or
.BR \-\-stream ).
Edges are written to a temporary binary file
.RI ( edges.bin )
during Phase 1, then processed in two passes during Phases 2+3.  RAM usage
stays under ~2 GB even at N\~>\~10M.  The edge file is deleted after
processing.
.PP
Mode selection is automatic based on available system RAM (via
.BR sysinfo ),
configurable via
.IR causal_set.toml ,
or overridable with flags.
