.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH MODULES
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SS "diamond \(em Phase 1: Vacuum Generation"
Poisson sprinkling in a 4D causal diamond + Hasse diagram construction.
Two tiers: sparse A\(S2 transitive reduction (N\~\(<=\~15k) and direct
geometric construction via the Occupied Cell Index (N\~>\~15k).
.TP
.BI "sprinkle(" n ", rng) \(-> (Vec<[f64;4]>, f64)"
Rejection-samples
.I n
points inside |t|\~+\~r\~\(<=\~T/2 with T\~=\~(24N)\u1/4\d giving
density \(*r\~\(~~\~1.
.TP
.BI "build_hasse_sparse(" pts ") \(-> (coords, adj_head, adj_data, momentum)"
Full causal closure \(-> sparse A\(S2 reduction.  Edge (i,j) is a Hasse
link iff A\(S2[i,j]\~=\~0.  Used for N\~\(<=\~15,000.
.TP
.BI "build_hasse_direct(" pts ") \(-> (coords, adj_head, adj_data, momentum)"
Direct geometric construction using the OCI (Occupied Cell Index) \(em a
spatial indexing paradigm that replaces naive geometric shell enumeration
(96% empty cells) with per-time-layer lists of occupied cells, queried
via binary search.  Three termination valves: Valve 1 (degree cap at
MAX_HASSE_DEGREE), Valve 2 (Alexandrov volume short-circuit: all causal
candidates transitively blocked \(-> break), Valve 3 (adaptive dry-shell
termination).
.TP
.BI "stream_edges_to_file(" n_total ", chunk_size, path, seed)"
Streaming variant that writes Hasse edges to disk using a sliding window,
for N too large to fit in RAM.  Output format: continuous stream of
(u32,\~u32) in little-endian.
.TP
.BI "sprinkle_chunk(" n_expected ", t_min, t_max, half_t, rng, start_idx)"
Poisson-sprinkle points into a time-slab [t_min,\~t_max].  Used
internally by the streaming path.
.PP
Key concepts:
.RS
.TP
.B GridPoint
A spacetime event quantised onto an integer lattice for cache-coherent
traversal.  Points are sorted by cell index so that spatially nearby
events are contiguous in memory.
.TP
.B OCI (Occupied Cell Index)
Paradigm shift from geometric to spatial indexing.  Builds per-time-layer
lists of occupied cells, sorted by X coordinate, queried via binary
search.  Reduces inner-loop cost from O(shell_volume) to
O(occupied_cells).
.TP
.B Termination Valves
Three valves control the dt-shell search.
.B "Valve 1 (Degree Cap):"
A node with \(>=\~MAX_HASSE_DEGREE (15) descendants has fully populated
its causal shadow; further links are redundant.
.B "Valve 2 (Alexandrov Short-Circuit):"
If every causal candidate in a dt-shell is transitively blocked (the
Alexandrov set between u and v is non-empty), further shells have
strictly larger Alexandrov volume and will also be blocked.  Breaks
immediately when degree \(>=\~1.
.B "Valve 3 (Dry-Shell Termination):"
One dry dt-shell (no causal candidates) with \(>=\~2 existing
descendants triggers cutoff.
.RE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "skyrmion \(em Phase 2: Kuratowski Contraction"
Pure integer topology \(em zero floating-point.  Core identification \(->
Causal Prism (K\d2,N\u bipartite) detection \(-> threat contraction \(->
generation classification.
.PP
Algorithm:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Core selection: top 10% of nodes by Hasse degree.
.IP 2.
Causal Prism formation: forward-forward 2-hop search.  For each core
node u with out-degree \(>=\~3 (minimum valence pruning), traverse
u\~\(->\~w\~\(->\~v to collect pole candidates.  Candidates v with
in-degree\~<\~3 are skipped before the belly intersection.  Belly =
children(u)\~\(*e\~parents(v); if |belly|\~\(>=\~3, the pair forms a
K\d2,N\u Prism.  Greedy best-partner selection maximizes N per pole.
.IP 3.
Threat contraction: any external node connected to BOTH poles AND \(>=\~2
intermediates is merged into the higher-degree pole.
.IP 4.
Generation classification: Prisms classified by bit-packed topological
signature [q\d0\u,q\d1\u,q\d2\u,q\d3\u] (quartile bulk momentum across
all components: origin, destination, and intermediates).
.RE
.TP
.BI "apply_defect(" n ", adj_head, adj_data, bulk_momentum) \(-> DefectResult"
Finds Causal Prisms (K\d2,N\u bipartite structures with belly nodes),
classifies them by topological signature into generations, performs threat
contraction, and builds the defect CSR by adding pole-completion edges.
.TP
.BI "process_streaming(" n_total ", chunk_size, path, seed) \(-> SpectralResult"
Out-of-Core variant.  Three-pass analysis: Pass 1 reads edges.bin to count
degrees and compute bulk momentum, Pass 2 builds core-induced CSR and runs
Causal Prism detection + generation classification, Pass 3 builds directed CSR
for causal flux measurement.
.PP
.B DefectResult
struct fields:
.RS
.TP
.B vac_head, vac_data
Vacuum Hasse CSR (row pointers + column indices).
.TP
.B def_head, def_data
Defect CSR after threat contraction + Prism pole-completion edges.
.TP
.B vacuum_core
Core node indices (top 10% by degree) in the vacuum graph.
.TP
.B defect_core
Core node indices surviving threat contraction.
.TP
.B gen1_nodes
Generation 1 Prism node indices (most abundant signature, electron-like).
.TP
.B gen2_nodes
Generation 2 Prism node indices (second most abundant, muon-like).
.TP
.B gen3_nodes
Generation 3 Prism node indices (third most abundant, tau-like).
.TP
.B anti1_nodes
Anti-Generation 1 Prism node indices (CPT conjugate, positron-like).
.TP
.B sterile_nodes
Sterile prism node indices \(em prisms with N\~>\~5 intermediates (dark
matter candidates, Conjecture C6).  Gravitationally active but
electromagnetically silent.
.TP
.B merge_into
Merge map: merge_into[i] = canonical node for node i.  For threat-absorbed
nodes, points to the absorbing Prism pole.
.RE
.\" ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SS "spectral \(em Phase 3: Spectral Dimension"
Random walk return probability measurement.  Two tiers: eigendecomposition
(exact, N\~\(<=\~3k by default; adjustable via
.BR \-\-eigen\-cutoff )
and Monte Carlo walkers (above the cutoff).
.TP
.BI "spectral_dimension(" steps ", p_vals) \(-> Vec<f64>"
d\dS\u(t) = \-2\~d(ln\~P)/d(ln\~t) via centred finite differences.
.TP
.BI "run_walkers(" adj_head ", adj_data, starts, steps, seed) \(-> Vec<f64>"
Run W independent lazy-walk walkers in parallel (50% stay, 50% move to
random neighbour).  Parallel via Rayon.  Strict Finitism: all internal
accumulation uses u64 integer arithmetic; the single f64 division
count\~/\~W occurs only at the final return.
.TP
.BI "run_transmission_walkers(" ... ") \(-> (Vec<f64>, Vec<f64>)"
Directed walkers (mandatory move along causal arrow).  Measures
transmission flux between particle generations (attraction and repulsion).
Same u64 integer accumulation as run_walkers.
.TP
.BI "compute_eigen(" n ", rows, cols, steps, core) \(-> SpectralResult"
Exact P(t) = N\u\-1\d \(*S \(*l\dk\ut from eigendecomposition of
S\~=\~D\u\-1/2\dAD\u\-1/2\d.  Complexity: O(N\(S3).
.TP
.BI "compute_monte_carlo(" n ", rows, cols, steps, core, n_w, rng) \(-> SpectralResult"
Monte Carlo P(t) from random walkers.  Builds CSR adjacency internally.
Complexity: O(W\(mut), independent of N.
.TP
.BI "compute_monte_carlo_csr(" n ", head, data, steps, core, n_w, rng) \(-> SpectralResult"
Zero-copy variant \(em avoids rebuilding adjacency when CSR is already
available from Phase 2.  This is the hot path for large N in-memory runs.
.TP
.BI "build_adj_list(" n ", rows, cols) \(-> (Vec<u32>, Vec<u32>)"
Build sorted undirected adjacency list in CSR format from edge lists.
.PP
.B SpectralResult
struct fields (14 total):
.RS
.TP
.BR p_global ", " ds_global
Return probability and spectral dimension from uniformly random starting
positions.  Probes global geometry.
.TP
.BR p_local ", " ds_local
P(t) and d\dS\u from walkers starting exclusively on core nodes.
Sensitive to topological defects.
.TP
.BR p_gen1 ", " ds_gen1
P(t) and d\dS\u for Generation 1 K\d4\u nodes (electron-like).
.TP
.BR p_gen2 ", " ds_gen2
P(t) and d\dS\u for Generation 2 (muon-like).
.TP
.BR p_gen3 ", " ds_gen3
P(t) and d\dS\u for Generation 3 (tau-like).
.TP
.BR p_anti1 ", " ds_anti1
P(t) and d\dS\u for Anti-Generation 1 (positron-like, CPT conjugate).
.TP
.BR flux_attraction
Directed transmission probability: Gen1 \(-> AntiGen1 (opposite charge).
.TP
.BR flux_repulsion
Directed transmission probability: Gen1 \(-> Gen1 (same charge).
.TP
.BR flux_attr_norm
Normalized attraction flux: flux_attraction / |targets_attraction|.
Isolates intrinsic per-node coupling strength (Conjecture C3).
.TP
.BR flux_repu_norm
Normalized repulsion flux: flux_repulsion / |targets_repulsion|.
.TP
.BR p_sterile ", " ds_sterile
P(t) and d\dS\u for walkers starting on sterile prism nodes (N\~>\~5
intermediates).  Conjecture C6: these are gravitationally active but
electromagnetically silent (dark matter candidates).
.TP
.BR ds_global_std ", " ds_local_std ", " ds_gen1_std ", " ds_gen2_std ", " ds_gen3_std ", " ds_anti1_std ", " ds_sterile_std
Population standard deviation of d\dS\u across M realisations.
Empty (vec![]) when M\~=\~1.  Provides error bars for publication figures.
.TP
.BR flux_attraction_std ", " flux_repulsion_std
Population standard deviation of causal flux across M realisations.
.RE
