.SS "memory \(em RAM-Aware Mode Selection"
Detects available system RAM, estimates memory requirements, and
recommends in-memory or streaming mode.
.TP
.BI "load_config(" dir ") \(-> Config"
Load configuration from a TOML file, or return defaults.  Searches for
.I causal_set.toml
in the given directory first, then falls back to the current working
directory.
.TP
.BI "ensure_config(" dir ")"
Write the default config file if it doesn't already exist.
.TP
.BI "recommend_mode(" n ", cfg) \(-> (ExecMode, available, estimated)"
Recommend an execution mode based on config + available RAM vs estimated
usage.  The estimate accounts for concurrent realisations.
.TP
.BI "prompt_mode(" recommended ", available, estimated, cfg) \(-> ExecMode"
Prompt the user to confirm or override the recommended execution mode.
.TP
.BI "estimate_memory_bytes(" n ") \(-> u64"
Heuristic peak memory estimate: N\~\(<=\~3k uses ~N\(S2\(mu24 bytes;
3k\~<\~N\~\(<=\~50k uses ~N\(mu2000; N\~>\~50k uses ~N\(mu500.
.TP
.BI "max_concurrent_runs(" n ") \(-> usize"
Default concurrency: 2 for N\~>\~10M, 4 otherwise.
Overridable via
.BR \-\-threads .
.TP
.BI "available_ram_bytes() \(-> u64"
Detect available system RAM in bytes via
.BR sysinfo .
.PP
.B ExecMode
enum:
.B InMemory
or
.BR Streaming .
.PP
.B Config
struct:
.B max_ram_bytes
(hard ceiling, 0 = auto),
.B safety_fraction
(0.0\(en1.0),
.B output_dir
(default directory).
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I N
Number of spacetime events (default: 5000).
.TP
.I M
Ensemble realisations (default: 10).
.TP
.I output_dir
Directory for results (default: current directory or
.I causal_set.toml
setting).
.TP
.B \-\-stream
Force streaming mode (low RAM, writes edges to disk).
.TP
.B \-\-inmemory
Force in-memory mode (fast, needs sufficient RAM).
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " u64
Base seed for deterministic runs.  Each realisation uses seed + i.
Default: system clock nanos (real entropy).  The chosen seed is printed
at startup so non-seeded runs can be reproduced.
.TP
.BI "\-\-threads " usize
Maximum parallel realisations.  Default: auto (2 for N > 10M in-memory,
4 otherwise; streaming capped at CPU count or 8).
.TP
.BI "\-\-epsilon " f64
Topological error tolerance \(*e for the Causal Resolution Theorem.
Default: 0.01.
.TP
.BI "\-\-tmax " usize
Maximum diffusion time.  Default: 15.
.TP
.BI "\-\-eigen\-cutoff " N
Eigendecomposition threshold.  Graphs with N \(<= cutoff use exact
eigendecomp; larger graphs use Monte Carlo walkers.  Default: 3000.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.\" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.SH CONFIGURATION
Place a
.I causal_set.toml
in the working directory (auto-generated on first run if absent):
.PP
.nf
# Hard limit on RAM (GB). 0 = auto-detect from system.
max_ram_gb = 0

# Fraction of available RAM considered safe (when auto-detecting).
safety_fraction = 0.70

# Default output directory for results and streaming edge files.
output_dir = "."
.fi
