.SH "EXPECTED RESULTS"
.SS "Spectral Dimension"
.TP
.B "Vacuum (global)"
d\dS\u diverges toward ~15.79 at late diffusion times (boundary
saturation of the unstructured bulk).
.TP
.B "Defect (with K\d4\u matter)"
d\dS\u stabilises at ~8.36 (topological retention \(em the K\d4\u knot
traps probability flow).
.TP
.B "Coupling constant"
\(*a\dtrans\u \(~~ 0.31, consistent with the observed strong coupling at
the tau mass scale.
.SS "Generation Classification"
K\d4\u cliques are classified by their topological signature (normalised
bulk momentum vector):
.TS
tab(|) allbox;
lb lb lb
l l l.
Generation|Physics Analogue|Signature
Gen1|Electron-like|Most abundant [M\d0\u,M\d1\u,M\d2\u,M\d3\u]
Gen2|Muon-like|Second most abundant
Gen3|Tau-like|Third most abundant
AntiGen1|Positron-like|CPT conjugate of Gen1
.TE
.SS "Causal Flux"
Directed walker transmission probabilities measure electromagnetic-like
interactions:
.TP
.B Attraction
Gen1 \(-> AntiGen1 (opposite charge, positive flux).
.TP
.B Repulsion
Gen1 \(-> Gen1 (same charge, lower transmission).
